    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d912">

                <pb facs="0860" n="756" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg756"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/6508.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Vice Consul at
                            Nogales to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Nogales</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-03-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 5, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>It is reported that the Congress of the State of Sonora decided today that it can
                    not accept the Provisional Government.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d912-f1"/> Bridges
                    are being destroyed by order of the State Government to prevent Federal troops
                    from arriving at Hermosillo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowman</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d912-f1" n="1" xml:id="d912-f1-content">
                <p>Confirmed by the Consul on March 6.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
